====== SKY SR102 ======

{{section>meta:infobox:broadcom_wifi#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

{{section>meta:infobox:broadcom_dsl#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

The Sky SR102 (Black) is an 400MHz dual-core [[https://www.broadcom.com/products/broadband/xdsl/bcm63168|Broadcom]] MIPS-based ADSL2+/VDSL2 router with 802.11bgn wireless and ADSL2+ support. It has a 4-port switch (3x LAN, 1x WAN) and (1x ADSL2+/VDSL2 port), The wireless antenna is integrated in the device but can be replaced with any half mini PCIe module.

There was also a re-branding of the same model and size with a NOW TV Green Logo. This is a NR701
[[https://i.imgur.com/5Cq38Sd.jpg]]

  * SR102 GPL Source code: [[http://www1.sky.com/opensourcesoftware/SkyHub/sky_hub_downloads.html]]
  * NR701 GPL Source code: [[http://www1.sky.com/opensourcesoftware/NowTvHub/NowTv_hub_downloads.html]]
  * Manufacturer's / Distributor's site: [[http://www.sky.com/shop/broadband-talk/]]

The NowTV Hub Two (model NR801) is also based on this design with a similar layout of UART serial pins.

